cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (8.709-Octave, 0.0905-37.86 um) Space-Lyman to Spitzer Thermal-IR, Gemini GHOST, VLT X-shooter/GIRAFFE/FEROS Optical-IR Laser, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um, HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um),
  ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS, HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, Gemini GHOST
  BLUE+RED 0.348-1.061 um with simultaneous sky-IFU veto, OHP SOPHIE, OHP ELODIE,
  CFHT ESPaDOnS, MPG/ESO FEROS, VLT FLAMES/GIRAFFE HR), far-red (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS),
  3-arm simultaneous UVB+VIS+NIR (VLT X-shooter 0.2989-2.4790 um), near-infrared YJH
  (NIRPS_HE), thermal J/H/K (VLT CRIRES+), SDSS APOGEE-2 H-band (up to N=26 visits),
  simultaneous YJHK (CFHT SPIRou APERO 0.7.295), JWST space thermal-IR (NIRSpec G235H/G395H,
  MIRI LRS, MIRI MRS Ch1-4), and Spitzer IRS SL+LL (5.20-37.86356 um) laser, curved/periodic
  multi-epoch drift, greenhouse CCF, Dyson waste-heat vs. silicate-belt discrimination, and
  periodic frequency-comb technosignatures (0.0905-37.86356 um, 8.709 unbroken octaves across
  25 spectrographs / 33 arms; 401 unique stars and 2,392 archival exposures totaling
  721.4813 h across V3.0-V5.3 + COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler across
  133 orbital campaigns, 26 N>=4 curved/periodic drift campaigns across D095 + Archive Q/T,
  Spitzer IRS 6-gas CCF & Dyson vs. silicate discrimination across 18 targets, simultaneous
  GHOST HDU[4..5] sky-IFU vetting + deterministic Stage-2 physical triage, and uniform all-sky
  COMB_V4_1 filtering across 441 stacks), unified with 1.4 GHz Parkes/GBT radio searches and
  TESS photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle closure across a 401-system synthesis
  (0 verified ETI detections; 0.0973 W HST_STIS Proxima Cen, 0.14238 kW JWST_NIRSPEC_G395H
  CWISEPJ1935, 0.20533 kW JWST_MIRI_LRS Luhman 16AB, 5.79094 kW GEMINI_GHOST GD 71, 37.57452 kW
  SDSS_APOGEE2 GJ 3801, 947.72011 kW SPITZER_IRS HD 151288, and 47 panchromatic bridges across
  706 cells alongside 161 <10 pc stars with 1.74941 kW median limit).
